    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my bosch dishwasher is showing an e15 error code. i checked the manual but im not really sure what to do. how do i check the leak sensor and dry out the base?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To check the leak sensor, locate it under the lower kick plate, usually at the kick plate's innermost corner. Gently pry the plate off and visually inspect for any blockages, liquids, or debris. Turn off the dishwasher and let it air dry completely before reinstalling the plate. However, it's recommended you unplug the dishwasher first.\n\nAs for drying the base, you can use a towel or soft cloth to pat the area dry. To prevent mineral buildup, you can also wipe the base with a mixture of equal parts water and white vinegar. Make sure the area is completely dry and clean before reinstalling the kick plate and sensors.",
      "source": "target",
